@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "zendesk.frontend"

Feature: KB Article Permissioning
	Frontend testing for viewing the Zendesk KB articles as various users

Teardown:
	* I teardown users with the following userExternalIds from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Enduser1 |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds from zendesk.liferay.com
	| 12341234 |

Scenario: View Fast Track Article as Guest
	Guests should be able to view all fast track article content available to guest users.

	Given I go to the zendesk page URL "/hc/en-us/articles/360037464812"
	And I accept all cookies
	Then I should be able to view the KB article title "Unable to startup the server: NPE while loading configurations from database"
	And I should be able to view the KB article fast track section
	And I should be able to view the KB article "issue" section header
	And I should be able to view the KB article "issue" section content
	And I should be able to view the KB article "environment" section header
	And I should be able to view the KB article "environment" section content
	And I should be able to view the KB article "resolution" section header
	And I should not be able to view the KB article "resolution" section content
	And I should not be able to view the KB article vote controls
	And the KB article "resolution" section should be gated
	And I should be able to view the KB article sign in message with sign in button

Scenario: View Fast Track Article as Customer
	Customers should be able to view all fast track article content available to customer users.

	Given I create an organization with the following values
	| Status           | Approved                   |
	| Name             | Frontend Org Name 1        |
	| Tags             | liferay_dxp,liferay_portal |
	| Shared Tickets   | true                       |
	| Shared Comments  | true                       |
	| SLA              | Gold                       |
	| Tier             | T4                         |
	| Support Region   | US                         |
	| Support Language | English                    |
	| External ID      | 12341234                   |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name         | Zendesk Enduser1                    |
	| Tags         | osb_customer                        |
	| Password     | zendeskqauser                       |
	| Role         | End-user                            |
	| Access       | Organization                        |
	| Email        | zendesk.enduser1@zendesk.com.broken |
	| Phone Number | +1 (555) 555-5555                   |
	| Organization | Frontend Org Name 1                 |
	| Language     | English                             |
	| Time Zone    | Pacific Time (US & Canada)          |
	| External ID  | Enduser1                            |
	And I log into zendesk as "zendesk.enduser1@zendesk.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I wait for "10" seconds
	And I go to the zendesk page URL "/hc/en-us/articles/360037464812"
	And I accept all cookies
	Then I should be able to view the KB article title "Unable to startup the server: NPE while loading configurations from database"
	And I should be able to view the KB article fast track section
	And I should be able to view the KB article "issue" section header
	And I should be able to view the KB article "issue" section content
	And I should be able to view the KB article "environment" section header
	And I should be able to view the KB article "environment" section content
	And I should be able to view the KB article "resolution" section header
	And I should not be able to view the KB article "resolution" section content
	And I should not be able to view the KB article vote controls
	And the KB article "resolution" section should be gated
	And I should be able to view the KB article subscription message with subscription link

